  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an **even** integer NNN and an integer KKK.\n\nGenerate an array AAA of size NNN such that:\n\n\n1≤Ai≤1051 \\le A_i \\le 10^51≤Ai​≤105 for all 1≤i≤N1\\le i \\le N1≤i≤N;\nThe number of **odd** elements in the array is same as the number of **even** elements.\nThe sum of all elements of the array is KKK.\nIf multiple such arrays exist, print any. If no such array exists, print −1-1−1 instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the size of the array and the required sum.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, NNN space-separated integers, denoting the array AAA satisfying the given conditions.\n\n\nIf multiple such arrays exist, print any. If no such array exists, print −1-1−1 instead.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105, NNN is even",
      "1≤K≤1091 \\leq K \\leq 10^91≤K≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 5\n4 1\n4 20",
        "output": "4 1\n-1\n3 4 5 8",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Consider the array A=[4,1]A = [4, 1]A=[4,1]. It contains 111 even as well as 111 odd element. Also, the sum of elements of the array is 4+1=54+1=54+1=5.\nTest case 222: It can be proven that there exists no array which satisfies the given conditions.\nTest case 333: Consider the array A=[3,4,5,8]A = [3, 4, 5, 8]A=[3,4,5,8]. It contains 222 even as well as 222 odd elements. Also, the sum of elements of the array is 3+4+5+8=203+4+5+8 = 203+4+5+8=20."
      }
    ]
  },
